msgid "``RestrictPublicChannelManagement``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1985
msgid "``RestrictPrivateChannelManagement``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1986
msgid "``RestrictPublicChannelCreation``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1987
msgid "``RestrictPrivateChannelCreation``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1988
msgid "``RestrictPublicChannelDeletion``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1989
msgid "``RestrictPrivateChannelDeletion``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1990
msgid "``RestrictPrivateChannelManageMembers``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1991
msgid "``EnableTeamCreation``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1992
msgid "``EnableOnlyAdminIntegrations``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1993
msgid "``RestrictPostDelete``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1994
msgid "``AllowEditPost``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1995
msgid "``RestrictTeamInvite``,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1996
msgid "``RestrictCustomEmojiCreation``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:1998
msgid ""
"The behavior of the ``config.json`` setting ``PostEditTimeLimit`` has "
"been updated to accommodate the migration to a roles based permission "
"system. When post editing is permitted, set ``\"PostEditTimeLimit\": -1``"
" to allow editing anytime, or set ``\"PostEditTimeLimit\"`` to a positive"
" integer to restrict editing time in seconds. If post editing is "
"disabled, this setting does not apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2002
msgid ""
"If using Let's Encrypt without a proxy server, the server will fail to "
"start with an error message unless the :ref:`Forward80To443 "
"<administration-guide/configure/environment-configuration-"
"settings:forward port 80 to 443>` ``config.json`` setting is set to "
"``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2005
msgid ""
"If forwarding port 80 to 443, the server will fail to start with an error"
" message unless the :ref:`ListenAddress <administration-guide/configure"
"/environment-configuration-settings:web server listen address>` "
"``config.json`` setting is set to listen on port 443."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2008
msgid "v4.6.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2008
msgid ""
"If using Let's Encrypt without a proxy server, forward port 80 through a "
"firewall, with the :ref:`Forward80To443 <administration-guide/configure"
"/environment-configuration-settings:forward port 80 to 443>` "
"``config.json`` setting set to ``true`` to complete the Let's Encrypt "
"certification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2012
msgid "v4.4.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2012
msgid ""
"Composite database indexes were added to the ``Posts`` table. This may "
"lead to longer upgrade times for servers with more than one million "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2014
msgid ""
"LDAP sync now depends on email. Make sure all users on your AD/LDAP "
"server have an email address or that their account is deactivated in "
"Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2016
msgid "v4.2.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2016
msgid ""
"Mattermost now handles multiple content types for integrations, including"
" plaintext content type. If your integration suddenly prints the JSON "
"payload data instead of rendering the generated message, make sure your "
"integration is returning the ``application/json`` content-type to retain "
"previous behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2019
msgid ""
"By default, user-supplied URLs such as those used for Open Graph "
"metadata, webhooks, or slash commands will no longer be allowed to "
"connect to reserved IP addresses including loopback or link-local "
"addresses used for internal networks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2022
msgid ""
"This change may cause private integrations to break in testing "
"environments, which may point to a URL such as http://127.0.0.1:1021/my-"
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2024
msgid ""
"If you point private integrations to such URLs, you may whitelist such "
"domains, IP addresses, or CIDR notations via the :ref:`Allowed Untrusted "
"Internal Connections <administration-guide/configure/environment-"
"configuration-settings:allow untrusted internal connections>` "
"configuration setting in your local environment. Although not "
"recommended, you may also whitelist the addresses in your production "
"environments. See :ref:`documentation to learn more <administration-"
"guide/configure/environment-configuration-settings:allow untrusted "
"internal connections>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2029
msgid ""
"Push notification, OAuth 2.0 and WebRTC server URLs are trusted and not "
"affected by this setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2031
msgid ""
"Uploaded file attachments are now grouped by day and stored in ``/data"
"/<date-of-upload-as-YYYYMMDD>/teams/...`` of your file storage system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2033
msgid ""
"Mattermost `/platform`` repo has been separated to ``/mattermost-webapp``"
" and ``/mattermost-server``. This may affect you if you have a private "
"fork of the ``/platform`` repo. `More details here "
"<https://forum.mattermost.com/t/mattermost-separating-platform-into-two-"
"repositories-on-september-6th/3708>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2036
msgid "v4.0.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2036
msgid "(High Availability only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2038
msgid ""
"You must manually add new items to the ``ClusterSettings`` section of "
"your existing ``config.json``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2040
msgid "v3.9.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2040
msgid ""
"Old email invitation links, password reset links, and email verification "
"links will no longer work due to a security change. Team invite links "
"copied from the Team Invite Link dialog are not affected and are still "
"valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2043
msgid "v3.8.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2043
msgid "A change is required in the proxy configuration. If you’re using NGINX:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2046
msgid ""
"Open the NGINX configuration file as root. The file is usually "
"``/etc/nginx/sites-available/mattermost`` but might be different on your "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2047
msgid "Locate the line: ``location /api/v3/users/websocket {``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2048
msgid "Replace the line with ``location ~ /api/v[0-9]+/(users/)?websocket$ {``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2050
msgid ""
"If you are using a proxy other than NGINX, make the equivalent change to "
"that proxy's configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2052
msgid ""
"You need to verify settings in the System Console due to a security-"
"related change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2054
msgid "Go to the the GENERAL section of the System Console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2055
msgid "Click **Logging**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2056
msgid ""
"Make sure that the **File Log Directory** field is either empty or has a "
"directory path only. It must not have a filename as part of the path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2058
msgid ""
"Backwards compatibility with the old CLI tool was removed. If you have "
"any scripts that rely on the old CLI, they must be revised to use the "
":doc:`new CLI  </administration-guide/manage/command-line-tools>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2061
msgid "v3.6.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2061
msgid "Update the maximum number of files that can be open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2063
msgid "On RHEL6 and Ubuntu 14.04:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2064
msgid ""
"Verify that the line ``limit nofile 50000 50000`` is included in the "
"``/etc/init/mattermost.conf`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2065
msgid "On RHEL7 and Ubuntu 16.04:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2066
msgid ""
"Verify that the line ``LimitNOFILE=49152`` is included in the "
"``/etc/systemd/system/mattermost.service`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2068
msgid "(Enterprise Only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2070
msgid ""
"Previous ``config.json`` values for restricting Public and Private "
"channel management will be used as the default values for new settings "
"for restricting Public and Private channel creation and deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2073
msgid "v3.4.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2073
msgid ""
"If public links are enabled, existing public links will no longer be "
"valid. This is because in earlier versions, existing public links were "
"not invalidated when the Public Link Salt was regenerated. You must "
"update any place where you have published these links."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2082
msgid "Additional upgrade notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2086
msgid ""
"Upgrading the Microsoft Teams Calling plugin to v2.0.0 requires users to "
"reconnect their accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2087
msgid ""
"Mattermost plugins built with Go versions 1.22.0 and 1.22.1 do not work. "
"Plugin developers should use Go 1.22.2 or newer instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2088
msgid ""
"Keybase has stopped serving Mattermost's Ubuntu repository signing key. "
"If you were using it, update your installation scripts to retrieve the "
"key as mentioned in our :doc:`Linux deployment documentation "
"</deployment-guide/server/deploy-linux>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2089
msgid ""
"We recommend avoiding the use of MySQL 8.0.22 as it contains an `issue "
"with JSON column types <https://bugs.mysql.com/bug.php?id=101284>`_ "
"changing string values to integers which is preventing Mattermost from "
"working properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/important-upgrade-notes.rst:2090
msgid ""
"When upgrading to Mattermost 7.x from a 5.x release, upgrade to 5.37.10 "
